# PostgreSQL connection string for local development and `next build`: the local
# database `ramhal`, filled by `npm run db:restore-local` (docs/DECISIONS.md §5).
# Never a Neon host — the Payload config refuses one when APP_ENV=development,
# unless a production one-off script sets ALLOW_PRODUCTION_ONE_OFF=TASK-NN on its
# own command line (docs/RECOVERY.md); never put that variable in this file.
# Use your own database user; Homebrew's local Postgres accepts any password, and
# a non-empty one keeps the diagnostics no-password-leak test meaningful.
DATABASE_URI=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/ramhal

# A SEPARATE connection string, required to run the test suite (vitest.setup.ts) —
# tests never fall back to DATABASE_URI above, on purpose. The local database
# `ramhal_test`, which the tests write to freely; a `*.neon.tech` host is always
# refused.
TEST_DATABASE_URI=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/ramhal_test

# This app's own public URL — no trailing slash. Used to build the Google
# sign-in redirect URI, which Google matches against the exact string
# registered in the Cloud console (src/lib/serverUrl.ts). Required in every
# environment, even when Google sign-in itself is not configured.
SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Random string used to sign Payload's auth tokens. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Required by scripts/dev-migrate.mjs (npm run migrate:create, which writes a
# migration file after a schema change) —
# see the security note atop src/app/(payload)/api/dev-migrate/route.ts.
# Local development only. Never set this in a production environment: its
# absence is one of two independent things that keep that route inert there.
# Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
DEV_MIGRATE_SECRET=

# Which deployment this is: development | demo | production. Required — the
# application refuses to start without it, so a forgotten variable can never
# quietly become "development". Separate from NODE_ENV, which only says whether
# the build is optimised: a deployed demo is NODE_ENV=production, APP_ENV=demo.
#   development  local work
#   demo         a public demonstration; every page carries a permanent banner
#                saying no real payment is taken
#   production   the live shop; the mock payment provider is refused
# It is also read while pages are prerendered, so set it for `next build`, not
# only for `next start`: a build records its APP_ENV and the server refuses to
# start under a different one.
APP_ENV=development

# Where uploaded media (book covers) is stored, in Cloudflare R2 (bucket
# ramhal-media). Three modes:
#   none set          uploads go to the local media/ folder (an offline setup)
#   S3_PUBLIC_URL     ONLY this one: read-only. Files are served from that address
#   alone             (the bucket's r2.dev URL) and uploads are refused, so a local
#                     environment can never write to production's bucket. Use this
#                     for local development.
#   all six           read-write — Vercel production only. S3_ENDPOINT is
#                     https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com, S3_REGION is
#                     "auto", and the key is scoped to the one bucket.
# Any other combination is an error. Uploads go directly from the browser, so the
# bucket's CORS policy (infrastructure/r2/media-bucket-cors.json) must allow the
# deployed admin origin.
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_PUBLIC_URL=
S3_REGION=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Which payment provider handles checkout. "mock" is a demo stand-in that
# marks orders paid without any real payment. It is allowed when APP_ENV is
# development or demo, and the application refuses to start with it when APP_ENV
# is production (src/lib/payment/paymentConfiguration.ts). "paypal" is the
# first real provider (docs/DECISIONS.md §7) — set the four PAYPAL_* variables
# below when using it.
PAYMENT_PROVIDER=mock

# PayPal adapter. Required together
# when PAYMENT_PROVIDER=paypal (src/lib/payment/paypalConfig.ts); irrelevant
# otherwise. From a PayPal Developer app (developer.paypal.com) — client id
# and secret from the app itself, webhook id from the webhook subscription
# created against this app's own /api/webhooks/paypal URL. PAYPAL_ENV is
# "sandbox" or "live" — independent of APP_ENV, which says which deployment
# this is, not which PayPal credentials it happens to hold. Never commit
# real values; sandbox credentials only until a live cutover is a separate,
# deliberate decision.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox

# Google sign-in for the admin panel (docs/DECISIONS.md §10). Required
# in every environment, local development included: local (email+password)
# login is fully disabled, so Google is the only way into /admin and the
# application refuses to start without both variables set
# (src/lib/auth/googleSignIn.ts). From the OAuth client named "ramhal-admin"
# in the "machon-ramhal" Google Cloud project.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated list of the only email addresses that may ever obtain an
# admin session, by any login path — local password, Google, or REST
# /api/users/login alike (src/collections/hooks/allowOnlyListedAdmins.ts).
# Required in every environment; the application refuses to start without
# it, exactly like a missing DATABASE_URI. It lives here and not in a
# collection because an attacker holding a session must not be able to
# edit it, and adding a person must not require a commit.
ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS=

# Optional hosted PayPal donation page. Leave unset until the institute's
# verified URL is available; the donation page then shows a clear, disabled
# placeholder instead of sending visitors to an unverified payment target.
# It becomes active only when APP_ENV=production, because a demo deployment
# promises that no money can change hands. Accepted hosts are paypal.com and
# paypal.me (including their subdomains).
PAYPAL_DONATION_URL=

# A read-only credential for the R2 bucket ramhal-backups. Used by GET
# /api/diagnostics (lets the app answer "are backups running" without any ability
# to write or delete one) and by `npm run db:restore-local`. All
# five or none (src/lib/backupReaderConfig.ts); unset entirely in local
# development, where there is nothing to report. This is a DIFFERENT,
# narrower-scoped credential than the one .github/workflows/backup.yml
# writes with — that one is a GitHub Actions secret, never an application
# environment variable, and is never written to this file either.
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=
BACKUP_S3_REGION=
BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
